神经学家正在研究如何操控人的思维。
Neuroscientists are learning how to take over our minds.

10
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:50,730
我们会有一天失去自我和灵魂么？
Will we someday lose control of our bodies and souls?

11
00:00:50,730 --> 00:00:54,450
僵尸末日有可能发生吗？
Is a zombie apocalypse possible?

12
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:04,710
空间，时间，生命本身。
Space, time, life itself.

13
00:01:06,790 --> 00:01:11,380
宇宙的奥秘，尽在穿越虫洞。
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

14
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:21,380
僵尸末日可能发生吗？

15
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:26,190
根据海地的民间传说，
According to Haitian folklore,

16
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:29,540
有些牧师拥有一种神奇的粉末...
certain priests had magical powders...

17
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:34,060
这种粉末能将死尸...
[ Thunderclap ] That could transform a corpse...

18
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:36,260
变成自己的傀儡。
into a puppet.

19
00:01:36,270 --> 00:01:40,740
现在的流行文化把僵尸传说
Our popular culture has turned that zombie legend

20
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:43,440
看做是世界末日：
into an apocalyptic nightmare,

21
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:46,740
一种传染性病毒将人类
a contagious virus that turns the infected

22
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:50,030
变成腐烂着的暴力怪物。
into violent monsters with rotting flesh.

23
00:01:50,030 --> 00:01:51,560
[ 雷鸣 ]
[ Thunderclap ]

24
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:54,170
只要被咬一口，
We are all just one bite away

25
00:01:54,170 --> 00:02:00,040
人们就会变成丧尸。
from joining the mindless legions of walking dead.

26
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:02,790
当然这些都是虚构的。
All of these are myths, of course.

27
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:04,080
[ 雷鸣 ]
[ Thunderclap ]

28
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:08,180
但每个传说都有现实依据，
But every myth has a grain of truth.

29
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:09,600
我们的这些想象
Could our imaginations

30
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:13,690
是否在启示着未来？
be telling us something about our future?

31
00:02:13,690 --> 00:02:15,420
[ 雷鸣 ]
[ Thunderclap ]

32
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:17,920
Freeman: 很久之前，
Freeman: A long time ago,

33
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:19,690
我和朋友们看了一场电影...
my friends and I saw a movie... [ Door creaks ]

34
00:02:19,690 --> 00:02:22,260
却让我们噩梦连连...
that gave us nightmares... [ All gasp ]

35
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:24,230
就是"木乃伊。"
"The Mummy."

36
00:02:24,230 --> 00:02:26,110
电影中，
[ Children screaming ] In that story,

37
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:28,480
古老的魔法将死者复活。
ancient magic made a corpse walk the earth again.

38
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:34,620
现实中会存在这样的怪物吗？
Could such a mindless monster ever exist in the real world?

39
00:02:39,110 --> 00:02:42,410
David Hughes是一位昆虫学家，
David Hughes is an entomologist.

40
00:02:42,420 --> 00:02:44,750
他有很长一段时间
He has a long history

41
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:47,750
都在研究这方面的黑暗科学。
with the dark side of that science.

42
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:49,000
当我还是孩子时，
When I was a kid

43
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:51,060
我感染了一种真菌，
I had a rather personal relationship with a fungus.

44
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:53,390
起初我们并不知道它是什么，
We didn't know exactly what it was at the beginning,

45
00:02:53,390 --> 00:02:55,130
几个月之后，
and over the course of months,

46
00:02:55,130 --> 00:02:58,400
那种真菌爬满了我的头皮，
this fungus creeped its way across my scalp,

47
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:00,180
我的半个头都秃了。
uh, making me half bald.

48
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,600
Freeman: David活了下来，
Freeman: David survived,

49
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:07,690
但感染这种真菌还不是最糟糕的。
but his fungus was not the worst nature has cooked up.

50
00:03:07,690 --> 00:03:12,140
一些真菌侵蚀宿主的身体
Some funguses turned the bodies of their hosts into piles of rot

51
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:15,480
并控制宿主的大脑。
and enslave their minds.

52
00:03:17,670 --> 00:03:20,540
David是前沿的真菌专家，
David is the foremost expert on a fungus

53
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:24,260
特别研究能够控制宿主的真菌，
that turns its victims into the walking dead,

54
00:03:24,260 --> 00:03:28,990
准确的说是到处爬的僵尸。
or to be more accurate, the crawling dead.

55
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
同地球上的所有生物一样，
The fungus, like all organisms on the planet,

56
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,210
这种真菌也有学名，
has a scientific name.

57
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:35,550
它叫偏侧蛇虫草菌,
This one's called ophiocordyceps unitlateralis.

58
00:03:35,550 --> 00:03:38,440
通俗的叫法是僵尸蚂蚁菌。
But colloquially, it's known as the zombie ant fungi.

59
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:40,860
Freeman:蚂蚁觅食时，
Freeman: While foraging for food,

60
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:42,270
不经意间
an unsuspecting ant

61
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:45,980
会沾上僵尸真菌的孢子。
will pick up a spore of the zombie fungus.

62
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:49,510
真菌的孢子穿透蚂蚁的身体，
The fungus bores through the ant's body.

63
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:52,650
感染蚂蚁的大脑并在其中繁殖，
It multiplies and infects the ant's brain,

64
00:03:52,650 --> 00:03:53,990
而且它会释放
where it releases

65
00:03:53,990 --> 00:03:56,740
一些控制大脑活动的化学成分。
powerful mind-controlling chemicals.

66
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:01,460
僵尸蚂蚁则会咬住叶片的背面，
The zombified ant bites the underside of a leaf

67
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:03,530
然后死去，
and dies.

68
00:04:03,530 --> 00:04:06,580
蚂蚁其实早已死亡。
Well, sort of.

69
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:09,200
死亡对寄生真菌来说是个开始。
Death is really the starting point for the parasite.

70
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:11,220
真菌需要
Fungi are rather interesting

71
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:14,090
它们的宿主死掉，
in that they require the host to die,

72
00:04:14,090 --> 00:04:17,710
这样就能在宿主的身体组织中生长繁殖。
and then, from its tissues, they grow and they reproduce.

73
00:04:17,710 --> 00:04:19,010
这时，
And so, at this stage,

74
00:04:19,010 --> 00:04:22,380
这只蚂蚁就被完全的改变了。
the whole ant body is completely transformed.

75
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,550
Freeman: 僵尸蚂蚁菌控制着
Freeman: The zombie ant fungus continues to control

76
00:04:26,550 --> 00:04:28,600
蚂蚁的思维，
the dead creature's mind,

77
00:04:28,610 --> 00:04:32,390
使蚂蚁一直咬住树叶。
keeping the insect's jaw locked onto the leaf.

78
00:04:32,390 --> 00:04:33,740
之后真菌开始繁殖，
The fungus multiplies,

79
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:36,060
在蚂蚁的头颅中不断加压
building pressure inside the ant's skull

80
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:40,750
直到头部裂开。
until...it breaks open.

81
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:44,500
从头颅中伸出的菌丝会向空气中释放致命孢子
Out comes a fungal stock that sprays down deadly spores

82
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:48,010
接着感染下一批受害者，
on the fungus's next victims.

83
00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:50,680
如此不断循环下去。
The cycle repeats.

84
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:53,210
真菌的孢子会抛射出去，
The fungal spores need to be shot out, launched,

85
00:04:53,210 --> 00:04:56,800
从高处落到蚂蚁通常的觅食道路上，
from an area high above the foraging trail.

86
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:59,250
以此真菌逐渐进化出了
And so the fungus has evolved the ability

87
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:02,970
控制宿主大脑的能力。
to control the mind of its host.

88
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:07,430
Freeman: 巢穴对蚂蚁来说是洁净的，
Freeman: Inside their nests, ants are hygienic.

89
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:09,390
但当它们外出觅食时，
But when they're out foraging,

90
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:12,480
就容易受到感染。
they are vulnerable to infection.

91
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:15,700
David认为这种真菌进化出了
David believes the fungus evolved the ability

92
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:19,150
专门在蚂蚁脆弱时感染它们的能力。
to strike the ants during this moment of weakness.

93
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:23,910
而僵尸蚂蚁菌并不会感染我们，
The zombie ant fungus could never infect us.

94
00:05:23,910 --> 00:05:26,790
因为我们的大脑结构与蚂蚁不同，
Our brains are too different from those of ants.

95
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:31,380
但是否有类似的病原菌感染我们的大脑呢？
But could a similar pathogen ever find its way into our mind?

96
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:34,220
显然，真菌已经进化出
So fungi have clearly evolved the ability

97
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:36,750
控制动物行为的能力，
to control the behavior of animals.

98
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:41,730
我们的大脑也是动物的大脑，没有理由认为
Our brains are animal brains, and there's no reason,

99
00:05:41,730 --> 00:05:44,560
我们的行为就不会被操控。
theoretically, why we couldn't have our behavior controlled.

100
00:05:49,270 --> 00:05:53,270
如果控制人类大脑的病原菌真的存在，
Freeman: If a mind-enslaving pathogen ever strikes humanity,

101
00:05:53,270 --> 00:05:54,940
它极有可能会通过
it will most likely jump to us

102
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:58,340
我们的遗传学近亲传染给我们。
from our close genetic relatives.

103
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:05,480
微生物学家Kartik Chandran专职研究埃博拉病毒...
Microbiologist Kartik Chandran studies the Ebola virus...

104
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:10,460
这是一种极可怕的病原菌，
A pathogen from our worst nightmares.

105
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:11,960
感染几周后，
Within weeks of infection,

106
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:17,630
多数病人会因血液从身体孔洞中大量流失而死亡。
most patients leak blood from every orifice and die.

107
00:06:17,630 --> 00:06:20,180
Kartik领导的研究团队想要找出
Kartik is leading a team to find out

108
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:25,390
像埃博拉这样的致命病毒是如何进化的。
how deadly viruses like Ebola evolve to infect humans.

109
00:06:26,890 --> 00:06:30,680
我们知道埃博拉通常存在于蝙蝠体内，
As far as we know, Ebola lives in bats,

110
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,030
但是偶尔，
and every once in a while,

111
00:06:32,030 --> 00:06:34,850
这种病毒会由蝙蝠感染其他动物，
this virus can break out from bats into other animals,

112
00:06:34,850 --> 00:06:38,230
包括属于灵长类的猩猩和人类。
including primates and apes and humans.

113
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:45,070
Freeman: Kartik正在研究
Freeman: Kartik is investigating

114
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:49,290
埃博拉是如何从蝙蝠感染到我们人类的。
how Ebola made the jump from bats to us.

115
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:52,380
他的研究方式
He's imagining what it's like

116
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:56,670
就是从病毒角度模拟这个过程。
to be one of the microscopic bad guys.

117
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:59,200
[ Static, door creaks ]

118
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:00,870
人类的身体就像一座建筑，
The human body is a lot like a building

119
00:07:00,870 --> 00:07:02,760
细胞就是其中的房间，
where our cells are rooms.

120
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:07,060
病毒会破门而入感染我们。
Viruses infect us by breaking and entering.

121
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:11,600
你可能会问，为什么这个小房间
So you might ask me, why does this little room

122
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:13,400
要被锁起来？
in this storage facility have a lock?

123
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:14,990
答案是很明显的 --
And so the answer is obvious --

124
00:07:14,990 --> 00:07:17,390
为了防止无关人员进出，
because somebody needs to go in and out.

125
00:07:17,390 --> 00:07:19,860
锁起来是保护入口的一种方式，
This is an attempt to secure the entrance

126
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:22,830
只有经过授权的人才能进入。
so that only the authorized individuals can get in.

127
00:07:22,830 --> 00:07:24,110
细胞也是一样，
And cells are the same way.

128
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:26,060
细胞需要摄入一些物质，
You know, cells need to bring stuff in,

129
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:27,280
也要排出一些物质，
they need to export stuff,

130
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,450
病毒已经进化出了一些
and viruses have really evolved to exploit

131
00:07:29,450 --> 00:07:31,840
进入细胞的方式。
this sort of entry and access ways.

132
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:34,670
病毒会模仿一些细胞生存所必须的
Freeman: Viruses mimic the shape of nutrients

133
00:07:34,670 --> 00:07:36,540
营养物质的形态，
that the cell needs to survive,

134
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:39,960
就像是撬锁工具模仿钥匙的形状。
just like a lockpick mimics the shape of a key.

135
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,930
[ Click, door rattling ]

136
00:07:42,930 --> 00:07:45,220
一旦进入细胞，
Freeman: Once inside the cell,

137
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:48,750
病毒就会插入它自己的遗传密码，
the virus inserts its malicious genetic code.

138
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:51,940
宿主细胞就会变成一个被奴役的工厂，
The host cell becomes an enslaved factory,

139
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:55,140
用来大量生产病毒。
producing countless copies of the invader.

140
00:07:55,150 --> 00:07:57,400
[ Screeching sound ]

141
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,400
病毒大量繁殖后
A multiplying virus can build so much pressure

142
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:03,740
产生的压力足以使宿主细胞破裂...
inside the host cell that it explodes...

143
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:05,400
[ Explosion ]

144
00:08:05,410 --> 00:08:10,910
...喷出的大量病毒会接着感染其他细胞。
...ejecting millions of viral clones to infect other cells.

145
00:08:12,610 --> 00:08:16,000
为了从动物感染到人类，
For a virus to jump from animal to human,

146
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:19,750
病毒需要找到一种
it has to find a piece of biological machinery

147
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:22,950
动物和人类共有的细胞机制。
shared by both the animal and the human cell.

148
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:25,760
就像常见的病毒和寄生物一样，
Like you often see with viruses and other parasites,

149
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:29,030
它们进化出了控制某些细胞机制的能力，
they evolve to co-opt these common cellular mechanisms,

150
00:08:29,030 --> 00:08:32,300
埃博拉也是这样。
and Ebola has done just that.

151
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:34,350
Freeman: Kartik有一项非常重要的发现，
Freeman: Kartik made a groundbreaking discovery.

152
00:08:34,350 --> 00:08:40,520
埃博拉依赖一种叫Npc1的蛋白感染细胞，
Ebola relies on a protein called npc1 to infect cells.

153
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:45,530
Npc1共同存在于蝙蝠和人类细胞中。
NPC1 is found in both bat and human cells.

154
00:08:45,530 --> 00:08:48,200
[ Chirping ]

155
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:50,530
蝙蝠和人类虽然看起来不同，
Bats and humans may seem very different,

156
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:55,540
但两者细胞的分子机制却十分类似，
but their cells use remarkably similar molecular machinery.

157
00:08:55,540 --> 00:09:00,010
大多数能感染蝙蝠的病毒也能感染人类，
Most viruses that infect bats can also jump to humans.

158
00:09:00,010 --> 00:09:05,100
而病毒需要做的就是找到那些通用钥匙。
All a virus has to do is find those common keys.

159
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:07,880
我认为这是概率事件，
So, I mean, I think it's a probability thing.

160
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:11,100
你越接近另一种生物，
The more closely related you are to another organism,

161
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:13,810
你感染病毒的概率越高。
the more likely you are to pick up a virus.

162
00:09:13,810 --> 00:09:15,840
Freeman: 有这么一种病毒
Freeman: A virus that turns human beings

163
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:22,350
能让人变成无意识的野蛮怪物...
into violent, unconscious monsters already exists...

164
00:09:22,350 --> 00:09:23,350
那就是狂犬病。
Rabies.

165
00:09:23,350 --> 00:09:25,120
得了狂犬病的人
People that have rabies

166
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:28,070
会在一段时间里表现暴躁、好斗，
go through a phase where they're highly violent and belligerent,

167
00:09:28,070 --> 00:09:29,320
并且口吐泡沫，
and they can foam at the mouth.

168
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:30,790
这些症状
These are changes that are --

169
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:33,020
会被病毒利用，
clearly seem to benefit the virus

170
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:35,040
病毒利用这些症状
in terms of its ability to spread

171
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:38,800
感染新的宿主。
from one infected host to a naive host.

