不断变着新的花样，
is constantly taking on new forms,

695
00:36:44,670 --> 00:36:47,930
但他们都有着一个共同点——
but they all have a common theme --

696
00:36:47,930 --> 00:36:53,160
感染者并不知道自己是僵尸。
the infected don't even know they are zombies.

697
00:36:53,170 --> 00:36:57,650
如果我们正是这场末日中的僵尸，
If, right now, we were zombies in the midst of an apocalypse,

698
00:36:57,650 --> 00:36:59,900
我们自己会知道吗？
would we even know it?

699
00:37:02,190 --> 00:37:05,140
[ Birds chirping ]

700
00:37:05,140 --> 00:37:06,990
神经科学家Scott Grafton
Neuroscientist Scott Grafton

701
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:09,480
认为像在高尔夫这样的运动中，
believes that in sports like golf,

702
00:37:09,480 --> 00:37:13,500
我们会变成僵尸。
it pays to be a zombie.

703
00:37:13,500 --> 00:37:14,790
我曾经看过一场锦标赛，
I was watching this tournament

704
00:37:14,790 --> 00:37:17,510
福兹·佐勒尔赢了那场比赛，
where Fuzzy Zoeller was winning.

705
00:37:17,510 --> 00:37:18,590
[ Whack ]

706
00:37:18,590 --> 00:37:20,460
广播员跑向他问：
Announcer runs up to him and says,

707
00:37:20,460 --> 00:37:22,760
“福兹，你是怎么做的？你怎么赢的？”
"Fuzzy, how did you do it? How did you win?"

708
00:37:22,760 --> 00:37:26,560
他说：“好吧，那是因为我一整周都不动脑子。”
He says, "Well, I've been brain-dead all week."

709
00:37:26,570 --> 00:37:28,000
[ Whack ]

710
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:32,840
Freeman:经过足够多的训练，一次好的挥杆是不自觉的，
Freeman: After enough practice, a good swing is automatic.

711
00:37:32,840 --> 00:37:36,860
实际上几乎所有的躯体动作
In fact, nearly everything that our bodies do

712
00:37:36,860 --> 00:37:40,010
都不需要思索，
requires little, if any, thought.

713
00:37:40,010 --> 00:37:43,180
几乎所有的行为都是无意识的。
Almost all of our actions are actually unconscious.

714
00:37:43,180 --> 00:37:46,730
我们假装能够控制自己的肌肉，
We can pretend we access our muscle.

715
00:37:46,740 --> 00:37:48,570
当我握着一个高尔夫球棍时，
You know, when I hold a golf club,

716
00:37:48,570 --> 00:37:49,990
我能抓住它，然后我能想：
I can grip it, and then I can think,

717
00:37:49,990 --> 00:37:53,990
好的，放松这块肌肉，拉伸这块肌肉，
okay, flex this muscle, extend this muscle,

718
00:37:53,990 --> 00:37:58,360
转动我的肩膀，扭动腰身，等等。
turn my shoulders, turn my waist, so forth.

719
00:37:58,360 --> 00:38:04,300
但实际上，我很难很难专门控制这些肌肉，
But actually, I have very, very poor access to those muscles.

720
00:38:04,300 --> 00:38:08,810
先确定想要什么样的结果更简单一些，
It's much easier to visualize what you'd like to happen,

721
00:38:08,810 --> 00:38:11,560
然后挥杆就行。
and the swing just takes care of itself.

722
00:38:12,710 --> 00:38:14,650
[ Whack ]

723
00:38:14,650 --> 00:38:17,710
Freeman:我们的大脑是目标指向的，
Freeman: Our brains are goal-oriented.

724
00:38:17,720 --> 00:38:19,720
我们只去思考最终目标，
We think of an end result,

725
00:38:19,720 --> 00:38:24,020
而身体则无意识的完成动作。
and our bodies mindlessly follow a program to achieve it.

726
00:38:24,020 --> 00:38:26,860
Freeman:对于Scott来说，
Freeman: For Scott, this is evidence

727
00:38:26,860 --> 00:38:30,410
这说明了我们的意志力并没有想象中的强，
that our willpower is not as strong as we think.

728
00:38:30,410 --> 00:38:34,830
一个好日子里一个人大约是97%的僵尸程度，
On a good day, I think we're about, uh...97% zombie,

729
00:38:34,830 --> 00:38:40,620
差日子就会有98%的程度，而剩余的2或3%
and on a bad day, 98% zombie, and the rest of the 2 or 3%

730
00:38:40,620 --> 00:38:42,910
代表了自由意志
is us having actually willful control

731
00:38:42,910 --> 00:38:45,080
能够控制日常行为。
over our daily activities.

732
00:38:47,300 --> 00:38:48,910
Freeman:Scott正在进行一种实验，
Freeman: Scott is running an experiment

733
00:38:48,910 --> 00:38:54,600
来控制受试者Misty那2%的自由意志，
to momentarily rob his subject, misty, of the other 2%.

734
00:38:56,220 --> 00:38:57,720
他使用的技术
He uses a technique

735
00:38:57,720 --> 00:39:00,810
叫做经颅磁刺激，
called transcranial magnetic stimulation,

736
00:39:00,810 --> 00:39:02,890
简称TMS，
or T.M.S., to induce

737
00:39:02,900 --> 00:39:05,150
用来产生她脑中一种无害电流。
a harmless electrical current in her brain.

738
00:39:05,150 --> 00:39:06,560
[ Click ]
Oh.

739
00:39:06,570 --> 00:39:10,200
TMS这种方法
T.M.S. is a method for

740
00:39:10,200 --> 00:39:13,990
能够短暂关闭你大脑中的一小部分的功能，
very briefly turning off a small part of your brain,

741
00:39:13,990 --> 00:39:17,710
我用铜线圈抵住你的头，
so it's a copper coil that goes against the skull,

742
00:39:17,710 --> 00:39:20,440
然后就能诱发电流，
and you induce a current through that,

743
00:39:20,450 --> 00:39:21,830
这段时间中，
and during that time,

744
00:39:21,830 --> 00:39:25,120
你的大脑相当于产生了损伤。
you essentially have a virtual lesion in your brain.

745
00:39:25,120 --> 00:39:26,120
[ Clicking ]

746
00:39:26,120 --> 00:39:27,950
Freeman:Scott将设备校正，
Freeman: Scott calibrates the device

747
00:39:27,950 --> 00:39:31,920
专门刺激控制右手的神经元，
by stimulating the neurons that control her right hand.

748
00:39:31,920 --> 00:39:37,460
然后再专门刺激顶叶皮层。
He then moves the device to focus on her parietal cortex.

749
00:39:39,460 --> 00:39:42,320
脑中这块区域的作用
This region of the brain is believed to be responsible

750
00:39:42,320 --> 00:39:46,570
是用来确保行为与意图一致的，
for making sure that our actions match our intentions,

751
00:39:46,570 --> 00:39:50,570
比如触摸红点。
like trying to touch an illuminated dot.

752
00:39:50,580 --> 00:39:53,240
第一轮实验中，
In the first round of Scott's experiment,

753
00:39:53,250 --> 00:39:56,080
并不使用TMS脉冲。
there is no T.M.S. pulse.

754
00:39:56,080 --> 00:39:57,950
一旦受试者的手开始移动，
As soon as their hand starts moving,

755
00:39:57,950 --> 00:40:02,200
我们马上把红点向右移动几英寸，
we jump that second light to the right a few inches,

756
00:40:02,210 --> 00:40:07,420
受试者的手会马上校正，
and their hand quickly corrects for that jump,

757
00:40:07,430 --> 00:40:11,660
顺利的按到第二个红点。
and it smoothly goes over and pursues that new location.

758
00:40:11,660 --> 00:40:13,460
Freeman:但在第二轮实验中，
Freeman: But in the second round,

759
00:40:13,470 --> 00:40:18,600
正当Misty的手指移动时，Scott电击了她的顶叶皮层。
right as misty's finger moves, Scott zaps her parietal cortex.

760
00:40:18,600 --> 00:40:19,840
哦！
Oh.

761
00:40:19,840 --> 00:40:21,560
Freeman:她的大脑并不能感觉到刺激，
Freeman: She doesn't feel the pulse

762
00:40:21,560 --> 00:40:23,340
但失去了意识行为能力
but loses the ability to consciously

763
00:40:23,340 --> 00:40:26,190
来纠正手指到第二个红点。
correct her action for a brief moment.

764
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:27,980
基本上他们的反应
They react, essentially,

765
00:40:27,980 --> 00:40:30,810
就像僵尸一样，想要指第一个红点，
as a zombie and go to the original location,

766
00:40:30,820 --> 00:40:32,150
而第二个红点出现后，
that second light,

767
00:40:32,150 --> 00:40:34,290
却无法纠正自己的动作到新的位置。
and they're unable to correct themselves on the fly.

768
00:40:34,290 --> 00:40:37,320
当我们把顶叶功能关闭后，
So when we turn off the parietal lobe,

769
00:40:37,320 --> 00:40:40,910
我们基本上就把一个人
we're essentially making a person a full zombie

770
00:40:40,910 --> 00:40:43,330
瞬间变成了僵尸。
for just a second or so.

771
00:40:43,330 --> 00:40:44,380
而在这个期间，
And during that time,

772
00:40:44,380 --> 00:40:45,530
他们仅是做出动作，
they're just carrying out a movement

773
00:40:45,530 --> 00:40:47,460
却无法继续控制这个动作了。
that they no longer can control.

774
00:40:49,470 --> 00:40:53,090
Freeman:Scott认为我们之所以进化成98%的僵尸，
Freeman: Scott believes we evolved to be 98% zombie

775
00:40:53,090 --> 00:40:56,340
就是要让大脑的智力部分
so that the intellectual parts of our brains

776
00:40:56,340 --> 00:40:58,280
从繁重而又花费大量时间的
could be freed up from thinking about the menial tasks

777
00:40:58,280 --> 00:41:01,450
各种大脑任务中释放出来，
that take up most of our time.

778
00:41:01,450 --> 00:41:04,480
对于进化到现在的人类来说，
For all of its evolutionary advantages,

779
00:41:04,480 --> 00:41:08,620
人脑具有高级智慧也是有代价的。
the intelligent human brain may come with a cost.

780
00:41:08,620 --> 00:41:11,540
我认为对于我们做的大多事情来说
I think we're a hair's breadth away from a zombie apocalypse

781
00:41:11,540 --> 00:41:14,830
现在距僵尸末日已经非常近了，
in the sense that most of what we do,

782
00:41:14,830 --> 00:41:16,460
甚至不知不觉就发生了。
we can accomplish without thinking about it.

783
00:41:16,460 --> 00:41:19,260
就只是想想上周你到底自主地
Just think about how many willful choices

784
00:41:19,270 --> 00:41:21,350
做了多少个选择，
you've made in the last week.

785
00:41:21,350 --> 00:41:23,600
或许只有一到两个，
It's probably maybe one or two.

786
00:41:23,600 --> 00:41:27,300
你做的其他事都是自发行为，
Everything else you did was essentially automatic behavior.

787
00:41:27,310 --> 00:41:30,940
那么现在你想做什么，就占用了那2%的自由意志，
So now you think of something, it takes away that last 2%.

788
00:41:30,940 --> 00:41:34,810
你早已准备并适应了像僵尸一样活着了。
You're already prepared to live as a zombie.

789
00:41:35,810 --> 00:41:38,450
Freeman:我们成年后，
Freeman: By the time we reach adulthood,

790
00:41:38,450 --> 00:41:41,370
日常生活中大多行为
most of our daily lives are spent engaging

791
00:41:41,370 --> 00:41:43,920
都基本不需要专门去思考。
in activities that require little conscious thought.

792
00:41:43,920 --> 00:41:48,790
但即使我们不能再清醒地做出决定，
If we were to lose our ability to make conscious decisions,

793
00:41:48,790 --> 00:41:51,930
生活也还和往常一样。
life just might continue as normal.

794
00:41:51,930 --> 00:41:54,880
当然，我们意识不到自己已经变成了僵尸，
Certainly, we wouldn't recognize it in ourselves,

795
00:41:54,880 --> 00:41:57,550
而可怕的是你能否辨认其他人
and the scary thing is whether you could recognize it

796
00:41:57,550 --> 00:41:59,300
是不是僵尸呢。
in anyone else.

797
00:41:59,300 --> 00:42:01,800
如果僵尸末日真会发生，
If there was a zombie apocalypse,

798
00:42:01,810 --> 00:42:04,510
我并不认为会像“僵尸世界大战”里描述的，
I don't think it would be like "World War Z."

799
00:42:04,510 --> 00:42:07,030
我们还会像平淡无奇的正常人一样，
I think we would be plain old normal human beings,

800
00:42:07,030 --> 00:42:09,060
只不过发生了一点点变化，
except we'd be a little bit different.

801
00:42:09,060 --> 00:42:11,680
这种改变更像是电影“天外魔花”，
We'd be more like "invasion of the body snatchers,"

802
00:42:11,680 --> 00:42:16,250
虽然我们每个人都在，但已经不再是真正的自己了。
where we're ourselves, but we're not ourselves anymore.

803
00:42:23,530 --> 00:42:27,680
人类热爱自由意志，
We humans love our free will.

804
00:42:27,680 --> 00:42:29,930
或许真会这么离奇，
As bizarre as it may seem,

805
00:42:29,940 --> 00:42:33,520
某种微小的寄生病菌或某种技术
it is entirely possible that a microscopic parasite

806
00:42:33,520 --> 00:42:35,810
很有可能变得无法控制，
or technology run wild

807
00:42:35,810 --> 00:42:40,810
夺走了我们如此珍惜的自由意志。
could take away the free will we cherish so dearly.

808
00:42:40,810 --> 00:42:43,160
而关于僵尸末日的所有说法
All of this talk of zombie apocalypse

809
00:42:43,170 --> 00:42:46,450
向我们提出了一个最终疑问——
raises one final question --

810
00:42:46,450 --> 00:42:51,540
为什么我们喜欢用半死不活吓唬自己？
why do we enjoy scaring ourselves half to death?

811
00:42:51,540 --> 00:42:53,760
也许这正说明了我们需要
Maybe that's what we need to do

812
00:42:53,760 --> 00:42:56,960
为最差的情况做准备。
in order to prepare for the worst.

813
00:42:56,960 --> 00:43:01,810
不过我才不怕，因为科学才是最好的防御武器。
I'm not scared, because science is our best defense.

